  "articleBody": "Hiring out new drywall installation should leave you with flawless walls, but simple oversights during the build can compromise your final paint job. Here are key pitfalls to watch for.\n\n- Skipping the framing check: Hanging drywall over bowed studs causes wavy walls. Avoid it by having your installer inspect and straighten framing first.\n- Jamming panel joints too tight: Forcing drywall sheets tightly together can crush edges and cause joint failure. Panels should be loosely butted.\n- Over-driving drywall screws: Sinking screws too deep breaks the face paper, losing holding power. Screws must sit slightly recessed without tearing paper.\n- Rushing dry times between coats: Applying joint compound before the base layer dries leads to shrinkage, cracks, and peeling. Allow ample drying time between coats.\n- Skipping proper surface priming: Painting directly onto fresh drywall mud leads to flashing and uneven sheen. Always seal mud and paper with drywall primer.\n\nCommon Mistakes to Avoid\nNever agree to a scope that skips dust containment or leaves out floor protection. A quality hanging crew plans for containment before hanging begins.\n\nIf you are planning an addition or basement finish across Denver or Aurora, reach out to HH Remodeling LLC at 303-505-0866 for dependable, hands-on service.",
